#basePath	Day4

:: BeginDay
@trigger    SceneReady
@boostScore 100
@who    Astrid

$call InitUpdateMasks()
$call ToggleDeskPicture()
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(CoordinateInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(PhotometerInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(BlueWavelength, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(InfraredWavelength, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(ColorInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(TemperatureInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(SpectrometerInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(HistoricalDataInstrument, true)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call StopOpenMode()

$call QueueMusic("Music.Moonthought", 3)
$call MoveToView("DocumentPuzzle")
$call SetInputState(false)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day41833")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs1
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day41833"
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day4ElijahPostcard")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs2
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day4ElijahPostcard"
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day4Martha")
$call SetInputState(true)

:: Day4ElijahPostcard
@trigger    DocumentInspectFlip
@when   documentId == "Day4ElijahPostcard"
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} Wait a minute. World’s End is a garden? 
{@Astrid} That must be what Elijah calls his station! World’s End, the garden of the golden apples. 
{@Astrid} It’s not about the world ending. It’s about love!
$call SetInputState(true)

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs3
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day4Martha"
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$call Wait(1)
$call SetInputState(false)
$call MoveToView("Right")
$call Wait(1)

{@Dad} Astrid, come in... Do you want the good news or the bad news first?
{@Dad} I know, I know. You can’t answer me. So I’ll just start with the good.
{@Dad} We’ve gotten our tech updated here at the South Pole. 
{@Dad} When Project Hercules is unlocked, we’ll actually be able to talk to each other! 
{@Dad} Plus, we’ll have access to all the data stored on the satellite. 
{@Dad} Star charts, meteor storms, black holes and supernovas... the whole recorded history of the night sky. 

{@Astrid} Wait a second... meteor storms? That’s what Elijah’s been so worried about. 
{@Astrid} Maybe we’ll be able to figure out when the storm is coming! 

{@Dad} So... onto the bad news. Elijah was supposed to be on his way home by now.
{@Dad} But I just heard from the STAR station in Kansas City.
{@Dad} They said they had one more job for him... a station near St. Louis that wasn’t on the map.
{@Dad} They’ve been cut off from supplies for a while. They need food and water. 
{@Dad} Elijah agreed to go and help them. That means it’ll be a bit longer before he gets home.

{@Astrid} Ugh. So much for solving this mystery together. Eleven cities in two months. The eleven labors of Elijah. 
{@Astrid} I guess it’s not quite as bad as Hercules... he ended up with twelve.
 
{@Dad} Anyway, you keep up the great work, Little Bear. We’ll talk soon. Over and out. 

{@Radio} Star HQ to Station Seven. IceCube is reading a high-energy neutrino emission from the area of the Taurus Constellation.
{@Radio} Identification of nearby celestial objects is requested. Uploading area of interest...
$call StartNeutrinoNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@trigger    NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@once

$call StopNeutrinoNavigation()
{@Radio} Neutrino Origin Detected
$call StartOpenMode()

:: PointsUpdated
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 2
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)

$call Wait(3)

$call StopOpenMode()
$call ClearMonitorSelection()

$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(2)
$call Wait(1)
$call MonitorUI->ShowCeresLogo()
// $call SetInstrumentUnlocked(HistoricalDataInstrument, true)
{@Radio} Congratulations on being awarded clearance level 5. You are now cleared to use the infrared module on your telescope.
{@Radio} Please reference your CERES Operator Manual for further information about your equipment.  $[Day4/Radio/l1_r_3(2)]
{@Radio} Thanking you for being an important part of the CERES Distributed Network of Citizen Observatories. Together, we will map the stars for a better tomorrow. $[Day4/Radio/l1_r_3(3)]
$call Wait(0.5)
{@Radio} Tuning you to the Ice Cube CERES headquarters for further instruction... $[Day4/Radio/l1_r_4]
$call MonitorUI->HideCeresLogo()
$call Wait(1)
$call StartPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: PuzzleNavigationComplete
@trigger    PuzzleNavigationComplete
@once

$call StopPuzzleNavigation()
$call StartPuzzleMode()

:: AndromedaDracoPuzzleComplete
@trigger    CorrectPuzzleSubmission
@when   puzzleName == "Andromeda"
@once

$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(false)
$call EndDay4->BeginCutscene()
$call Wait(3)
{@Astrid} Whoa. That’s it. It’s the dragon!
{@Astrid} I should’ve guessed. Elijah said “the dragon is coming.” It’s going to be a Draconid meteor storm!

:: EndDay
@trigger    CutsceneEnd
@when cutsceneId == "EndDay4"
@who    Astrid

$call LoadNextDay()